{"Allowing negative start_offset for previous cursors is incompatible with Django QuerySet slicing - when cursor.is_prev is true, this can generate slices like queryset[-10:20] which Django QuerySets don't support and will raise an error": 0.9414558410644531, "Accessing organization_context.member.has_global_access without guarding against a missing member can raise AttributeError for non-members when organization_context.member is None": 0.8427485823631287, "The trimming condition still uses offset instead of start_offset, which can desynchronize the overfetch logic - when offset != start_offset (e.g., after clamping), the condition len(results) == offset + limit + extra no longer matches the fetched range and can trim the extra record incorrectly": 0.8822540044784546, "The offset/extra trimming logic for cursor.is_prev assumes non-negative offsets, so when negative offsets are allowed this may produce incorrect slice boundaries or result removal": 0.9572664499282837, "The OptimizedCursorPaginator largely duplicates the existing BasePaginator.get_result flow with minor conditional changes, creating maintenance risk - should extract shared logic into reusable helpers or parameterize the existing paginator": 0.2919871211051941}